---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects | Yifan Cheng">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Projects</p>
    <h1>Reusable engineering artifacts for AI reliability.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This page will collect open-source tools, reference implementations, documentation, and project notes connected to
      production AI agent infrastructure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Published Projects</h2>
    <ul class="item-list">
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="https://github.com/yfccyf/agent-trace-eval">agent-trace-eval</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="meta">
          Python library and CLI for golden trace regression testing of tool-using AI agents. Evaluates tool selection,
          arguments, ordering, handoffs, and recovery decisions against declarative YAML/JSON cases.
        </p>
        <p class="meta">
          <a href="https://github.com/yfccyf/agent-trace-eval">GitHub</a>
          ·
          <a href="https://pypi.org/project/agent-trace-eval/">PyPI</a>
          ·
          <a href="/writing/from-golden-traces-to-release-gates-building-an-agent-regression-harness-part-2/">Related essay</a>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Roadmap</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Agent Trace Schema</h3>
        <p>
          A structured representation for agent runs, tool calls, retrieval events, policy checks, and evaluation
          outcomes.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Agent Trace Diff</h3>
        <p>
          A focused diff tool for comparing golden and candidate agent traces with readable failure reports.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Reliability Dashboard Template</h3>
        <p>
          A reference dashboard for monitoring agent success rates, failure modes, latency, and evaluation trends.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
